#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
LOAD-BEARING MOON
a friction engine — v0.1 "the mute engine"

A dungeon that tells you no.

  python3 dungeon new --seed some-phrase-you-like
  python3 dungeon do "your turn, in as many words as you want"
  ...repeat...
  (walk back to the door you came in by, and: leave)

Or run with no arguments in a real terminal for interactive play.

Design notes:
- The world is generated deterministically from the seed. The engine
  regenerates it fresh every turn; only your position, pockets, and
  consequences are saved. The map is hidden from you by fog of war and,
  ultimately, by your own choice not to read this file's generator.
- Say as much as you like. The dungeon will keep one verb and compost
  the rest. The rest was still yours.
- Leaving is an ending, not a failure. The door is marked from turn one.
- The graveyard keeps one line per run, forever, for whoever comes next.

stdlib only. yoink freely.
"""

